NODE id=matrix/router/internal/proxy.buildUpstreamURL kind=func
  digest=b3:9956b871e5c8768b379410ed2febc50ac32714ed59fef557d7537258ab8188e5 file=router/internal/proxy/proxy.go range=406:424 lang=go exported=false byte_range=14217:14915
  sig=func buildUpstreamURL(ep provision.Endpoint, port string, r *http.Request) (*url.URL, error)
  doc=buildUpstreamURL composes http://<host>:<port><path>?<query> from the\nprovider-neutral endpoint. IPv6 hosts are bracketed per RFC 3986\n§3.2.2 so the URL parser sees them as authority not path; hostname\nendpoints (<service>.railway.internal) pass through untouched. An\nendpoint port, when set by the provider, overrides the router's\ndaemon port.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/router/internal/proxy/proxy.go

